*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
*** Title: Mediation model (Figure 1) - what accounts for the SMSD gap between IWP Employees and AROP w/o IWP?
*** Treatment W: smd_grp (1 = IWP Employees, 0 = AROP w/o IWP), outcome Y: smd (SMSD rebuilt from 13 items)
*** Confounders X (in all models): year, age, sex, household type, education, region, urbanisation and health
***   (general health, limitation, chronic illness PH020); prior history only in the longitudinal data (not here)
*** Mediators M:
***   M1 current income   : income position inc_rel (% of poverty threshold); poverty gap = 100 - inc_rel, so not added separately
***   M2 income structure : share of social transfers (other than old-age/survivor) in disposable income, (HY020 - HY022) / HY020
***   M3 asset proxies    : tenure (HH021), capital income (HY090G > 0), rental income (HY040G > 0) - robustness only
***   M4 household        : other persons (18-64) in the household working >= 7 months, 0 / 1 / 2+ (as x_OTHW in the ladder)
***   Work intensity (RX040) is not used: it contains the person's own months of work, i.e. partly the treatment itself
*** Method: KHB decomposition (Karlson, Holm & Breen 2012), implemented by hand so that contributions can be summed per block
***   a_j = coefficient of W in OLS of mediator j on W + X
***   b_j = coefficient of mediator j in the logit of Y on W + X + all M (full model); c' = coefficient of W there (direct effect)
***   c   = coefficient of W in the logit of Y on W + X + residualised M (total effect, same scale) = c' + sum_j a_j * b_j (exact)
***   Reported: logit scale, share of the total gap (%), probability scale in pp (KHB-APE; block pp apportioned by the logit
***   shares) and in % of the predicted NEP rate; standard errors from the official khb command (Part G, delta method)
*** Parts: A setup | B mediators by group | C paths a and b | D ladder (gap after adding blocks) | E KHB main (M1, M2, M4)
***        | F KHB robustness (+ M3) | G standard errors with the official khb command
***        | G2 item-level decomposition: same model for each of the 13 SMSD items (which items does each mediator explain?) | H export
*** Health is a confounder (Figure 1). Set global HEALTH_ROLE to "M" to treat health as mediator block M5 instead.
*** Input: SILC_All_Years_Adjusted.dta | Output: Mediation_log.txt, sheets Med_paths, Med_ladder, Med_KHB, Med_items in 05_Deprivation_Results.xlsx
*** Requires: khb (installed automatically from SSC if missing)
*******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

